miRings: Mutable Instruments Rings (Emilie Gillet, MIT) as a Nebulae program.
Only the lines between nebconfigbegin and nebconfigend are read; this text is not.

Controls (change the osc: lines to move them, no compile needed):
  pitch    note, C1..C6 (knob + 1V/oct CV over 5 octaves)
  speed    FM, -12..+12 semitones
  blend    structure (also the chord of the sympathetic-string models)
  window   brightness
  density  damping
  start    position
  overlap  model: 0-5 resonators (modal, sympathetic, string, FM, quantized
           sympathetic, string + reverb), 6-11 string synth with fx
  size     polyphony 1..4
  reset    strum (button or gate)
  freeze   on: the left audio input excites Rings; off: Rings excites itself
  blend_alt (secondary controls) depth of the right audio input as FM,
           0..48 semitones at full scale (0 = off): an oscillator there
           modulates the pitch at audio rate (2 kHz, Rings' block rate)
  record_alt (secondary controls) mono: on = ODD + EVEN on both outputs
           (as the module with one cable), off = ODD left, EVEN right
A pitch change also strums. The OSC paths miRings knows are listed in
source/main.cc.

nebconfigbegin
run,miRings
oscport,3020
kernel,normal
blocksize,128
osc:pitch,/rings/note,24,84
osc:speed,/rings/fm,-12,12
osc:blend,/rings/structure,0,1
osc:window,/rings/brightness,0,1
osc:density,/rings/damping,0,1
osc:start,/rings/position,0,1
osc:overlap,/rings/model,0,11,int
osc:size,/rings/polyphony,1,4,int
osc:reset,/rings/strum,0,1
osc:freeze,/rings/internal_exciter,1,0
osc:blend_alt,/rings/fm_in,0,48
osc:record_alt,/rings/mono,0,1
nebconfigend
